# Design: Close Supervision archive page at /supervision

## Problem
The newsletter needed a public subscribe + archive surface before the
first send (scheduled 2026-10-27). The brand decided on the full name
"Close Supervision" with the sanctioned shorthand "supervision" for
constrained identifiers.

## Approach
Static prerendered page at src/pages/supervision.astro reusing the
existing NewsletterSubscribe component (which posts to the Resend
Audience via /api/subscribe). Issue metadata lives in typed
src/data/newsletter-issues.ts; adding an issue is one array entry and
the list sorts newest-first. No content collection was introduced —
the repo's collections are implicit (no src/content/config.ts), so a
plain data module follows the existing src/data idiom with less risk.

## Key Trade-offs
- Short URL /supervision vs /close-supervision: shorter for sharing
  and domain use; prose and from-name keep the full name.
- Archive links to the lead blog article (/4-minutes-to-book) rather
  than duplicating email bodies in the repo; the article is still
  draft:true, so the link 404s until launch morning.
- Brand rules live in ~/newsletter/BRAND.md outside the repo to keep
  subscriber-analysis references out of the public history.

